{
    "article_summary": "The article describes the organophotoredox catalytic enantioselective addition of N-acyl radicals to aldehydes using a commercially available chiral imidazolidinone organocatalyst. The study compares batch and continuous flow protocols, demonstrating that while yields remain modest (up to 52%), the flow process significantly enhances productivity (up to 60 times) and space-time yields (up to 113 times) without compromising enantioselectivity (up to 85% e.e.).",
